  "oracle": "pose_error_m is the Euclidean residual in metres of geometry_core estimate_pose_chamfer_v3_2 against the analytical scene constructed in geometry_core/test/test_pipeline_v3_2.cpp (RecoversFrontoParallelPoseOnSyntheticScene): coincident pinhole cameras, a flat depth plane at z = 2 m, and an RGB box centred on the principal point with half-size 300 by 40 px. Ground truth is that construction (tx = 0, ty = 0, tz = 2, yaw = 0), not a stored estimator output. Yaw is a rotation about the camera vertical axis, so its residual is converted with the box half-width at z = 2, which is 2/3 m per radian. A rejected pose scores 5 m, the stage-2 depth_max_m gate. latency_ms is the wall-clock time of the seed-0 call after one discarded warmup, built at -O3 with OMP_NUM_THREADS=1.",
